.Dd October 28, 2026
.Dt VINIT.CONF 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vinit.conf
.Nd vinit service file format
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Pa /etc/vinit/services/ Ns Ar name Ns Pa .conf
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Each file in
.Pa /etc/vinit/services
whose name ends in
.Pa .conf
defines one service for
.Xr vinit 8 .
The file name without
.Pa .conf
is the service name.
A service name starts with a letter, digit or underscore, and contains
only letters, digits and the characters
.Ql _.@- .
.Pp
The file has sections in square brackets, and lines of the form
.Ql key = value .
A line that starts with
.Ql #
or
.Ql \&;
is a comment.
A comment must be on its own line.
.Pp
The parser is strict.
.Xr vinit 8
rejects the whole file if it has an unknown section or key, a duplicate
key, an empty or malformed value, or a line longer than 1023 bytes.
It also rejects a file that is not owned by root, or that is writable
by group or others.
.Sh SECTION [service]
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm command = Ar path Op Ar arg ...
Required.
The command to run.
It never runs through a shell.
Words are separated by whitespace.
Double quotes group words, and inside them
.Ql \e"
and
.Ql \e\e
are the only escapes.
Outside quotes, the characters
.Ql \(aq \(ga $ \&| \&; & < > \e
are rejected.
The first word must be an absolute path.
To use a shell, write
.Ql command = /bin/sh -c \(dq...\(dq .
.It Cm name = Ar name
Optional.
Must match the file name.
.It Cm type = simple | oneshot
A
.Cm simple
service is a long-running process.
A
.Cm oneshot
service runs to completion; it is ready when it exits with status 0.
Default:
.Cm simple .
.It Cm stop_timeout_ms = Ar ms
Time between
.Dv SIGTERM
and
.Dv SIGKILL
when the service stops.
Default: 5000.
.It Cm ready_fd = Ar fd
Give the service the write end of a pipe as file descriptor
.Ar fd ,
from 3 to 1023.
The service stays
.Dq starting
until it writes a newline there.
Only for
.Cm type = simple .
.It Cm ready_timeout_ms = Ar ms
If the service is not ready after
.Ar ms ,
stop it and count the run as a failure.
Needs
.Cm ready_fd .
Default: 0, wait forever.
.It Cm critical = yes | no
If
.Cm yes
and the service fails,
.Xr vinit 8
starts an emergency shell.
Default:
.Cm no .
.El
.Sh SECTION [restart]
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm policy = no | on-failure | always
When to restart the service after it exits.
.Cm always
also repeats a successful oneshot.
Default:
.Cm no .
.It Cm delay_ms = Ar ms
Delay before the first restart.
The delay doubles after each consecutive restart, up to 60 seconds.
A run that lasts 10 seconds or more resets the count.
Default: 1000.
.It Cm limit = Ar n
Give up after
.Ar n
consecutive restarts.
Default: 0, never give up.
.El
.Sh SECTION [dependencies]
Each key takes a list of service names separated by spaces, and may be
repeated.
.Xr vinit 8
rejects unknown names and dependency cycles.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm requires = Ar name ...
Start these services first, and start this service only when they are
ready.
If one of them fails, this service fails too.
If one of them stops, this service stops too, and starts again when the
dependency is ready again.
.It Cm after = Ar name ...
Ordering only.
Wait while these services are starting or waiting to restart.
Do not wait for a service that has failed or stopped.
.El
.Sh SECTION [execution]
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm user = Ar name | uid
Run as this user, from
.Pa /etc/passwd .
.It Cm group = Ar name | gid
Run with this group instead of the user's primary group.
.It Cm working_directory = Ar path
Absolute path of the working directory.
Default:
.Pa / .
.It Cm env = Ar NAME Ns = Ns Ar value
Set an environment variable.
May be repeated.
.It Cm stdin = null | console
Default:
.Cm null .
.It Cm log = Ar name
Send standard output and standard error through a pipe to the standard
input of service
.Ar name ,
as runit log services do.
Implies
.Cm after = Ar name .
.El
.Sh SECTION [limits]
All keys are optional.
Each needs cgroup v2; without it, a service with limits fails to start.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm memory_max = Ar size
Memory limit in bytes, with an optional
.Cm K ,
.Cm M ,
.Cm G
or
.Cm T
suffix (powers of 1024).
.It Cm pids_max = Ar n
Limit on processes and threads.
.It Cm cpu_max = Ar percent Ns %
CPU limit as a percentage of one CPU.
.Ql 200%
is two CPUs.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/vinit/services -compact
.It Pa /etc/vinit/services
Service files.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[service]
command = /usr/sbin/sshd -D
stop_timeout_ms = 5000

[restart]
policy = on-failure
limit = 5

[dependencies]
requires = network

[execution]
log = sshd-log
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr vinit 8 ,
.Xr vinitctl 8
